# pikvm settings: shipped by stack/pikvm. Every setting pikvm reads.
#
# This machine's values go in ~/.config/pikvm/pikvm.local.env, beside this file (yours, never
# shipped). The environment wins over both: `PIKVM_HOST=root@kvm2 pikvm msd list` does what it
# says. Format: NAME=value, one per line, read and never sourced (only a leading ~/, or a value
# that is ~, is expanded, to $HOME; a value may be quoted). A commented line is the default used
# when nothing sets it. `pikvm config` is to list and set them; until it exists, edit
# pikvm.local.env.

# The PiKVM: an ssh alias or user@host (-H wins)
#PIKVM_HOST=root@pikvm
# Extra ssh options, e.g. "-p 2222 -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new"
#PIKVM_SSH_OPTS=
# The image `pikvm msd connect` presents: <storage dir>/<file>
#PIKVM_MSD_IMAGE=ventoy/ventoy.img
